DEV / SAMPLE KEY — NOT A PRODUCTION SIGNING KEY
================================================

`dev-sample.pub` (and, if present locally, `dev-sample.key`) are a throwaway
minisign keypair generated ONLY so the sign/verify pipeline in this directory
can be exercised end-to-end without touching any real Postern signing material.

Rules:

  * NEVER sign a real enterprise delivery with this key.
  * NEVER present anything signed with it to a customer as authentic.
  * The real enterprise signing key is OPERATOR-held and lives OUTSIDE this
    repository. It is never committed here.
  * A secret key (`dev-sample.key`) may exist in your local working copy for
    testing; it must not be committed and carries no trust.

This mirrors the project's honesty posture: signed != reproducible != attested,
and a signature only ever proves "the holder of THIS key produced these bytes".
